  ('GSP 102', 'Use of English II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Geography', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Part A: Basic Grammar: Introduction. The concept of grammar and its place in language teaching and learning. Parts of speech and their functions (treated in detail). Closed and open class items in parts of speech, Nominalization, Grammatical Structures: the phrase, the clause and the sentence. Elementary Clause Analysis, Sentence Types, Elements and Patterns. Agreement (Grammatical agreement, Notional agreement, Proximity agreement) Agreement with the correlatives. Direct and Reported Speech, Error typology identification and correction.

Part B: Varieties of writing. Introduction (The Meaning, Nature and Purpose of Writing, Writing Types or Genres and their Characteristics). The paragraph as the basic unit of an essay (Types, Development of the Paragraph, Methods of Paragraph Development, The thesis statement). Point of view and style in writing. Qualities of a good piece of writing: Form, Diction and Content in writing. The Mechanics of Writing: punctuation, spelling and capitalization.

Part C: Writing Genres - Planning and choosing your theme. Deciding your genre. Choosing and developing your plot. Point of view, setting and characterization. Using the language that works. Essay Writing — Narration, Description, Exposition and Argumentation. Technical Writing: Letter Writing, Memorandum Writing, Speech Writing, Agenda and Minutes, own story for practice, Computer-linked writing, types, style, language, and process.', '["Part A: Basic Grammar - The concept of grammar, Parts of speech, Grammatical Structures, Sentence Types, Agreement, Direct and Reported Speech, Error typology", "Part B: Varieties of writing - Meaning, Nature and Purpose of Writing, the paragraph as the basic unit of an essay, the thesis statement, Qualities of a good piece of writing, Mechanics of Writing", "Part C: Writing Genres - Planning and choosing your theme, plot, point of view, setting and characterization", "Essay Writing - Narration, Description, Exposition and Argumentation", "Technical Writing - Letter Writing, Memorandum Writing, Speech Writing, Agenda and Minutes"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Mechanical Engineering handbook'),
  ('GSP 106', 'Natural Science II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Geography', '100 Level', 'second', 2, '', '[]'::jsonb, 'Faculty of Social Sciences course handbook'),
  ('ECO 102', 'Principles of Economics II', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Geography', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Elementary principles of macroeconomics and microeconomics; National income determination; The circular flow of income; Injections, withdrawals and the multiplier; Income determination; consumption, saving and investment functions; Nature and features of money; The banking system and the supply of money; Money supply and price level; International trade; Exchange rate and comparative advantage; Foreign trade and domestic economy; Economic growth; Elementary notion of economic planning; Introduction to Marxist economic theory.', '["Elementary principles of macroeconomics and microeconomics", "National income determination", "The circular flow of income; Injections, withdrawals and the multiplier", "Income determination; consumption, saving and investment functions", "Nature and features of money", "The banking system and the supply of money", "Money supply and price level", "International trade; Exchange rate and comparative advantage", "Foreign trade and domestic economy", "Economic growth", "Elementary notion of economic planning", "Introduction to Marxist economic theory"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Economics handbook'),
  ('PSY 103', 'Determinants of Behaviour', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Geography', '100 Level', 'second', 2, 'Definition of learning. Types of learning: classical conditioning, operant conditioning, social learning, concept learning, etc. Measurement of learning and their uses. Complex learning: Learning set or learning-to-learn; insight. Brain substrates of learning; memory and artificial intelligence. Practicals.', '["Definition of learning. Types of learning: classical conditioning, operant conditioning, social learning, concept learning, etc", "Measurement of learning and their uses", "Complex learning: Learning set or learning-to-learn; insight", "Brain substrates of learning; memory and artificial intelligence. Practicals"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Psychology handbook'),
