  ('GLG 103', 'Basic and Applied Geology for Environmental and Physical Sciences', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Geography', '200 Level', 'first', 3, 'The earth and the solar system; internal structures and physics of the earth; important minerals and major rock types; geologic time-scale and geochronology; elements of earth history; relationship between geomorphic and structural features; weathering and erosion, gullying, landslide, floods, desert advance, and environmental pollution, and their control; outlines of the geology and mineral resources of Nigeria.', '["The earth and the solar system", "Internal structures and physics of the earth", "Important minerals and major rock types", "Geologic time-scale and geochronology", "Elements of earth history", "Relationship between geomorphic and structural features", "Weathering and erosion, gullying, landslide, floods, desert advance, and environmental pollution, and their control", "Outlines of the geology and mineral resources of Nigeria"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Geology handbook'),
  ('MTH 111', 'Elementary Mathematics I', 'University of Nigeria, Nsukka', 'Faculty of Social Sciences', 'Geography', '200 Level', 'first', 3, 'Elementary Set theory, subsets, union, intersection, complements. Venn diagrams, Real numbers, integers, rational and irrational numbers, mathematical induction, real sequences and series, theory of quadratic equations, binomial theorem. Circular measure, trigonometric functions of angles of any magnitude, addition and factor formulae. Complex numbers, algebra of complex numbers, the Argand Diagram, De Moivre''s theorem, $n$th roots of unity.', '["Elementary Set theory, subsets, union, intersection, complements", "Venn diagrams, Real numbers, integers, rational and irrational numbers, mathematical induction, real sequences and series, theory of quadratic equations, binomial theorem", "Circular measure, trigonometric functions of angles of any magnitude, addition and factor formulae", "Complex numbers, algebra of complex numbers, the Argand Diagram, De Moivre''s theorem, $n$th roots of unity"]'::jsonb, 'Department of Mathematics handbook'),
